// © Kizzy
//
// Kizzy – CRT Blueprint
// Candle Range Theory (CRT) detector across up to 3 higher timeframes.
//
// CRT models
//  1 · Classic CRT        C1 = range. C2 sweeps ONE side of C1 and closes back inside.
//  2 · Two Candle CRT     C2 is an opposite-colour candle with a big body that sweeps one side of C1
//                         (closing inside, or straight through the other side = "delivered").
//  3 · Multiple Candle    Any setup that needs 2+ more HTF candles after the sweep to reach TP2 (tagged "MC").
//  4 · Double Purge CRT   C2 sweeps one side, C3 sweeps the OTHER side, both close inside C1 → trade C3's reversal.
//  5 · Inside Bar CRT     Mother bar + 1..N inside bars, then a candle sweeps the mother bar and closes inside.
//
// Key levels – taken from a HIGHER TF than the CRT candle (top-down, Romeo style).
// The sweep wick must tap one (filter on by default) – shown as 🔑 tags.
//  OHP  Old High Purge     wick takes an older swing high, closes back below it        (bearish)
//  OLP  Old Low Purge      wick takes an older swing low, closes back above it         (bullish)
//  RB   Rejection Block    wick taps the wick zone (body → wick extreme) of an older swing candle
//  OB   Order Block        wick taps the last opposite candle before a displacement
//  FVG  Fair Value Gap     wick taps an open 3-candle imbalance
//  OCL  Open/Close Level   wick taps an older body (open/close) swing level, closes back on the other side
//  IFVG Inverse FVG        wick taps an FVG that price already closed through (polarity flipped)
//
// Time filter: 4H CRTs only when the sweep candle opens at 1am / 5am / 9am New York.
// LTF entry: Turtle Body Soup (TBS) on the chart timeframe while a CRT is active.
// Statistics table: TP1 / TP2 / stop rates per CRT type and for TBS entries.
// HTF bias: Bull CRT only when the sweep low is in DISCOUNT of the key-TF range, Bear only in PREMIUM.
//
// Targets: TP1 = 50% of the range, TP2 = opposite side of the range.
// Invalidation: price trades beyond the sweep candle's extreme before TP2.
//
// Alerts: Create Alert → Condition "Kizzy CRT" → "Any alert() function call".

//@version=6
indicator("Kizzy – CRT Blueprint", shorttitle = "Kizzy CRT", overlay = true, max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_boxes_count = 500)

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
